<Layout title="About" current="About">
  <section class="page">
    <h2>About Local Buzz ATX</h2>
    <p><b>What’s happening. Why it matters.</b></p>
    <p>Local Buzz ATX is a local news and community site for Austin, Round Rock, Georgetown, Hutto and the neighborhoods around Travis and Williamson counties. We point you to the original reporting, then add the plain-English “why it matters” so you can get through the day’s news fast.</p>

    <h3 class="fh" style="margin-top:22px">What you’ll find</h3>
    <p>News headlines that link to the original source. Practical guides. Technology and online-safety education. Community voices. And OMG!, our short, funny reactions to the day’s stories.</p>

    <h3 class="fh" style="margin-top:22px">Who we are</h3>
    <p>Our writers are real people with real opinions. They go by pen names, like Caleb on tech and security, and Tori on relationships, family and entertainment. Our guides come from the Local Buzz ATX in-house voice, and Mind the Marbles and OMG! are our lighter columns.</p>

    <h3 class="fh" style="margin-top:22px">How we use AI</h3>
    <p>We use AI tools to help draft, summarize and add reactions. We review our content, and headlines always link to the original reporting. OMG! lines are jokes, not news, and we don’t joke about crime, victims or politics.</p>

    <h3 class="fh" style="margin-top:22px">How we’re funded</h3>
    <p>We’re supported by advertising, sponsorships and affiliate links. When we recommend something and may earn a commission, we say so (see our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>). Sponsors don’t decide what we cover.</p>

    <h3 class="fh" style="margin-top:22px">Corrections</h3>
    <p>Found a mistake? Tell us and we’ll fix it and note the change. See our <a href="/corrections">corrections page</a>.</p>

    <AdRow />
  </section>
</Layout>
